{"step_index":1206,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T21:04:59Z","input_tokens":2559,"cache_read_tokens":111051,"output_tokens":1950,"thinking":"Deletion workers are failing to complete operations for several support cases, as shown by recent activity logs. The failures originate from the support platform. Analyzing the specific nature of these recorded events may reveal the root cause of the deletion failures.\n\n\nRedaction failures are directly linked to PII exposure and incomplete account deletions, as indicated by partial or failed operation results. The indexing logic incorrectly marks records as \"ABSENT\" even when deletions are only partially or unsuccessfully completed. Audit case status provides a clear distinction between complete and incomplete states, the former lacking violations and only having verification phases, while the latter includes findings, remediation, and verification phases with violations.\n\n\nThe cases with \"INCOMPLETE\" status and only the \"VERIFICATION\" phase arise because the expected account evidence file is missing, leading to an empty verification list within a specific auditing function. This absence causes the audit to be marked as \"INCOMPLETE\" even though the deletion was technically successful. The logic then fails to update to a completed verification phase. This results in an incorrect \"INCOMPLETE\" status despite successful deletion activity.\n\n\nCases with \"INCOMPLETE\" status, but only verification steps, indicate missing findings within the indexing process. Specific data flows and attachments were not correctly parsed, leading to their absence in the index. The parsing of deletion and redaction failures in system logs seems inconsistent with the presence of `PARTIAL` or `FAILED` states.\n\nA review of the cases where findings are missing is needed to understand the cause. The examination will include why items are parsed as \"PRESENT\" but not as findings. The processing differences between the initial and updated versions are under review using the `diff_all_cases.py` script to identify how data flows were missed, potentially related to parsing failures of specific attributes.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cd C:\\\\Users\\\\Pavan\\\\hackerrank-orchestrate-october26; Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Filter \\\"*pipeline*\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Search for pipeline files\""}}]}
